# Channel Three service flags. Installed by pi-setup.sh to /etc/default/channel3.
#
# systemd reads this file as KEY=value lines only. The one line it acts on is
# the CHANNEL3_FLAGS assignment at the bottom, which is appended to the
# ExecStart line in channel3.service.
#
# So do not uncomment the candidates below. They are bare flag text and systemd
# cannot parse them as lines. Copy the ones Phase 4 proves into the quoted value
# of the CHANNEL3_FLAGS assignment at the bottom, then restart the service:
#
#   sudo systemctl restart channel3
#
# The unit itself never changes.
#
# systemd splits CHANNEL3_FLAGS on whitespace and does no shell quoting, so no
# single flag may contain a space. None of the flags below need one.
#
# --root and --listen are already on the ExecStart line. Do not repeat them.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# mpv output. Phase 4 task 2 tries these in order until one plays full screen
# with no desktop running. Pi OS Trixie ships mpv 0.40, whose default Vulkan
# path has been reported to fail at 1080p, and --gpu-api=opengl fixes it.
# Use exactly one of the three groups.
#
#   --mpv-arg=--vo=gpu --mpv-arg=--gpu-context=drm --mpv-arg=--gpu-api=opengl --mpv-arg=--hwdec=no
#   --mpv-arg=--vo=drm
#   --mpv-arg=--vo=gpu-next --mpv-arg=--gpu-context=drm
#
# The Pi 5 has no H.264 hardware decoder, so --hwdec=no is honest rather than
# limiting. The television is a 720p panel; if software decode is thin at
# 1080p, cap ingest rather than scaling here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio. Use the first two on every Pi. The service user has no PipeWire
# session, so mpv's default output logs a PipeWire error and can fail outright
# on a cold boot when the service starts before the sound card is ready. On the
# first boot that happened, mpv refused every file. --ao=alsa goes straight to
# the hardware, and --audio-fallback-to-null=yes plays the picture silently
# rather than not at all if the sound card still is not there.
#
#   --mpv-arg=--ao=alsa --mpv-arg=--audio-fallback-to-null=yes
#
# Only if the HDMI output is not ALSA's default device. Phase 4 task 3 records
# the right name; `mpv --audio-device=help` lists them.
#
#   --mpv-arg=--audio-device=alsa/sysdefault:CARD=vc4hdmi0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Remote. The Flirc presents as a USB keyboard. Leave this off to let serve
# find the Flirc by name and fall back to any keyboard, or pin the device if
# autodetection picks the wrong one. Use the by-id path: it survives a reboot,
# /dev/input/eventN does not.
#
#   --input-device=/dev/input/by-id/usb-flirc.tv_flirc-event-kbd
#
# --no-input turns every key source off, which makes the channel unchangeable.
# Useful only when debugging a wedged remote.
#
#   --no-input

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Television power and volume over HDMI-CEC. The Samsung UN40H4005AF lists
# Anynet+ in its spec and ships with it off, under Menu, System, Anynet+.
# Turn --cec on only if Phase 4 task 7 got the television to answer cec-ctl.
# If it never answers, leave these off and let the universal remote do power
# and volume.
#
#   --cec
#   --cec-device=/dev/cec0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Startup channel. Default is the lowest numbered channel in the config.
# The value is the channel's id, the `id` field in its YAML, not the number
# typed on the remote.
#
#   --start-channel=trains

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A Please Stand By card that replaces the one built into the binary.
#
#   --standby=/srv/channel3/local/standby.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A different mpv binary. The default is whatever mpv is on PATH.
#
#   --mpv=/usr/bin/mpv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Home video uploads. A phone sends a clip to http://channel3.local/api/upload
# with this PIN in an X-Upload-PIN header; the clip is prepared in the
# background and appears on any channel whose sources name local/home. Unset or
# empty, there is no upload endpoint at all. This is an environment variable,
# not a flag, so it is a line of its own below CHANNEL3_FLAGS, and it never goes
# in the repository.
#
#   CHANNEL3_UPLOAD_PIN=1234

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The live line. Everything above is a comment; this is the only line systemd
# reads. A filled in example, still commented, then the empty one it ships with:
#
#   CHANNEL3_FLAGS="--mpv-arg=--vo=gpu --mpv-arg=--gpu-context=drm --mpv-arg=--gpu-api=opengl --mpv-arg=--hwdec=no --mpv-arg=--ao=alsa --mpv-arg=--audio-fallback-to-null=yes"

CHANNEL3_FLAGS=""
